# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-1 windows (the ship-5 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt, ORDER-W2.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the three runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-next-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory and, since NP9, with the output
# ceiling of its catalog entry; the keys are the same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix, replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader
# refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint, which is what their question (exactness of reuse against a cold twin of the same boot; the platform sequence) does not depend on.
# N1 (STOP; NP9's N1 on the candidate): ONE request at a time, 30,000 tokens, on Swift. warmup; concurrent8_steady (the profile's required eight-user check, which also
# proves the octo rounds still run); long_answer_prefix (one 4k real-code prompt asked at max_tokens 16,384 and then 30,000, both ignore_eos: the long answer must begin
# with the short one but for its last 512 characters - greedy decoding does not change with the ceiling); long_answer_solo_4k (a 4k prompt, 30,000 tokens, ignore_eos) and
# long_answer_solo_200k (a 200,000-token prompt as the server counts it, 30,000 tokens, ignore_eos: the request reserves 3,596 of the pool's 16,499 blocks). Each request is
# alone: every round is a lone-user padded round (NP1). CEILING READ: the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] request output budget 32768 for this checkpoint (its catalog entry;
# the profile says 16384)" and "[QWEN-C2] request contract installed: greedy, max_tokens <= 32768" (c2_smoke_check requires the second whenever a long-answer test ran), the
# checkpoint lines (c2_smoke_check --expect-checkpoint) and no "kv reservation too large" line. ANSWER READ (c2_smoke_check, long_answer_problems): every user of a
# long_answer test ends with finish "length" and exactly 30,000 tokens (ignore_eos, so the stop is the ceiling, not the model); fewer tokens at "length" is a server whose
# ceiling clamped the request. MEMORY READ: the output ceiling allocates no verifier capture, proposal bucket or page table (docs/tp4-np9-answer32k.md), so the DRAM lines
# are the candidate's own: no "dram backstop refused", no "dram admission hold" that the same prompts would not have drawn at 16,384, no engine-build failure, no "audit
# mismatch", no stall. READ also: the solo decode rate is recorded, never gated; the stream never stalls for the answer's 7 to 15 minutes (a gap over the profile's
# QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_MAX_DECODE_GAP_S, 8 s, is a fault). Stop rule: a request that ends short of 30,000 tokens, a prefix difference, a stall, any audit mismatch or a refusal
# line. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1,
# scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A
# rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): 75 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,long_answer_prefix,long_answer_solo_4k,long_answer_solo_200k
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
